  "staticMarkdownSelectors": [
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "Strokes: 4 \u00b7 Key (radical): \u5200 (no. 18), appearing as \u5202 on the right \u00b7 JLPT: N1 (community list)",
      "step": "kanji-01"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5208 concerns cutting growing things: mowing grass, clipping hair, or reaping crops. The native verb \u5208\u308b \u304b\u308b retains a cutting action; it is not a general word for every method of harvesting.",
      "step": "kanji-03"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology: Picture the two crossed strokes on the left as growth to be clipped beside the upright knife form \u5202 on the right. The indexing radical is \u5200; \u5202 is its right-hand form. This shape association is a memory aid, not a reconstruction of the character's history.",
      "step": "kanji-04"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "table",
      "target": "\u30ac\u30a4",
      "step": "kanji-09"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "table",
      "target": "\u5208\u9664 \u304c\u3044\u3058\u3087 \u2014 removal; cutting off; mowing",
      "step": "kanji-11"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "table",
      "target": "\u30ab\u30a4",
      "step": "kanji-12"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "table",
      "target": "\u5208\u9664 \u304b\u3044\u3058\u3087 \u2014 an alternative reading of the same word",
      "step": "kanji-14"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "table",
      "target": "\u304b.\u308b",
      "step": "kanji-15"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "table",
      "target": "\u5208\u308b \u304b\u308b \u2014 mow; clip; reap",
      "step": "kanji-17"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "Focus practice on \u304b\u308b. The two on readings are retained for recognition: JMdict records both \u304c\u3044\u3058\u3087 and \u304b\u3044\u3058\u3087 for \u5208\u9664, without a spelling or sense restriction separating them. This does not establish how often either is used. In \u5208\u308b, \u5208 supplies \u304b and \u308b is the written verb ending.",
      "step": "kanji-18"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5208\u308b \u304b\u308b \u2014 mow; clip; reap",
      "step": "kanji-20"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u7a32\u5208\u308a \u3044\u306d\u304b\u308a \u2014 rice reaping; rice harvesting",
      "step": "kanji-21"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "The object helps with the English translation: \u8349\u3092\u5208\u308b (\u304f\u3055\u3092\u304b\u308b) is mowing grass, \u9aea\u3092\u5208\u308b (\u304b\u307f\u3092\u304b\u308b) is clipping hair, and \u7a32\u3092\u5208\u308b (\u3044\u306d\u3092\u304b\u308b) is reaping rice plants. See the linked verb article for complete examples.",
      "step": "kanji-22"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5207, \"cut,\" has a broader range. Compare \u5208's crossed left strokes and separate upright \u5202 with \u5207's left part and bent \u5200 on the right.",
      "step": "kanji-24"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u4e43, \"thereupon; possessive no,\" \u51f9, \"concave; sunken,\" and \u51f8, \"convex; protruding,\" do not mean mowing or reaping.",
      "step": "kanji-25"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "Learn \u5208\u308b as a godan verb: \u5208\u308a\u307e\u3059 (\u304b\u308a\u307e\u3059), \u5208\u3063\u305f (\u304b\u3063\u305f), \u5208\u3089\u306a\u3044 (\u304b\u3089\u306a\u3044). These inflections do not add new dictionary readings.",
      "step": "kanji-26"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "Metadata: KANJIDIC2, 2026-11-02 snapshot. Word families: JMdict, entries 1209540, 1209550 and 1167840. Native verb usage: Digital Daijisen and Nikkoku, \u5208\u308b. The \u30ac\u30a4 compound is also recorded by Jitsu, \u5208\u9664; that heading does not independently verify \u30ab\u30a4.",
      "step": "kanji-27"
    },
    {
      "document": "kanji/\u5208.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5208\u308b \u304b\u308b \u2014 mow; clip; reap",
      "step": "karu-forward"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5208\u308b means to cut grass, hair, crops, or similar growth: to mow, clip, shear, or reap according to the object. It is a transitive godan verb. The thing cut takes \u3092; the polite form is \u5208\u308a\u307e\u3059 (\u304b\u308a\u307e\u3059), the past \u5208\u3063\u305f, and the negative \u5208\u3089\u306a\u3044.",
      "step": "karu-02"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5ead\u306e\u8349\u3092\u5208\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002 (\u306b\u308f\u306e\u304f\u3055\u3092\u304b\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002) - I cut the grass in the garden.",
      "step": "karu-03"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u590f\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u9aea\u3092\u77ed\u304f\u5208\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002 (\u306a\u3064\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u304b\u307f\u3092\u307f\u3058\u304b\u304f\u304b\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002) - Since it is summer, I had my hair cropped short.",
      "step": "karu-04"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u77ed\u304f describes the resulting short length in the second example.",
      "step": "karu-05"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5208 represents cutting or reaping. It supplies the native stem \u304b, followed by the kana ending \u308b. There is no multi-kanji compound to decompose.",
      "step": "karu-07"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5207\u308b (\u304d\u308b) is the broader verb for cutting. It works with many objects that do not suit \u5208\u308b, such as a sheet of paper. \u9aea\u3092\u5207\u308b, \"cut one's hair,\" does not specifically present the haircut as cropping or clipping.",
      "step": "karu-09"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "The object helps determine the English verb: \u8349\u3092\u5208\u308b is mowing or cutting grass, while \u7a32\u3092\u5208\u308b (\u3044\u306d\u3092\u304b\u308b) is reaping rice plants. Do not extend the English gloss \"harvest\" to every crop or method of gathering food. \u5208\u308b retains a cutting action, rather than simply collecting something that has grown.",
      "step": "karu-11"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "Dictionary: JMdict, entry 1209540, sense 1.",
      "step": "karu-12"
    },
    {
      "document": "words/\u5208\u308b.md",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "target": "\u5208 represents cutting or reaping. It supplies the native stem \u304b, followed by the kana ending \u308b. There is no multi-kanji compound to decompose.",
      "step": "karu-reverse"
    }
